CoreCLR on riscv64 (plan step V2.4): the JIT inlines thread static access through a fixed offset from the thread pointer where the runtime's TLS is static; WitOS's dynamic linker, musl's, gives libcoreclr.so, which the host dlopen opens, dynamic TLS alone, so the offset GetThreadStaticsVariableOffset computes (asmhelpers.S, the general-dynamic model on WitOS) is the current thread's and would be wrong for the others. CanJITOptimizeTLSAccess answers false for WitOS riscv64, as upstream answers for linux-musl arm64 for the same reason, and the JIT takes the helper calls.

--- a/src/coreclr/vm/threadstatics.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/vm/threadstatics.cpp
@@ -922,6 +922,10 @@
     // Optimization is disabled for linux/x86
 #elif defined(TARGET_LINUX_MUSL) && defined(TARGET_ARM64)
     // Optimization is disabled for linux musl arm64
+#elif defined(TARGET_WITOS) && defined(TARGET_RISCV64)
+    // Optimization is disabled for WitOS riscv64: the dynamic linker (musl's) gives the runtime, which the host dlopen
+    // opens, dynamic TLS alone, so the offset GetThreadStaticsVariableOffset returns is the current thread's, not every
+    // thread's.
 #elif defined(TARGET_FREEBSD) && defined(TARGET_ARM64)
     // Optimization is disabled for FreeBSD/arm64
 #elif defined(TARGET_ANDROID)
